-- title:
--   Smooth closed points of integral models: special fibre a DVR
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be an algebraically closed field, $A \subseteq L$ a valuation subring, and $F$ a field extension of $L$ which is a curve over $L$ in the project's sense: $F/L$ has principal divisors (every $f \neq 0$ is the datum of a degree-zero divisor whose value at each place $v$ is $\operatorname{ord}_v f$), each place of $F/L$ has residue field finite over $L$, and $\Omega_{F/L}$ is free of rank $1$ over $F$. Let $X$ be an integral scheme with a morphism $\mathrm{toBase} \colon X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ that is locally of finite presentation, and let $\varphi \colon F \xrightarrow{\sim} K(X)$ be a ring isomorphism compatible with the structure map, in the sense that for every $a \in A$ the element $\varphi(a \cdot 1)$ is the image of $a$ under $A \to \Gamma(X,\mathcal O_X) \to K(X)$ (germ at the generic point of the pullback of global sections along $\mathrm{toBase}$, composed with the inverse of the $\Gamma$–$\operatorname{Spec}$ adjunction isomorphism). Let $x \in X$ satisfy: $x$ lies over the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A$; the only $y$ with $x \rightsquigarrow y$ is $x$ itself (so $x$ is closed); and $x$ lies in the smooth locus of $\mathrm{toBase}$. Write $c \colon A \to \mathcal O_{X,x}$ for the analogous map into the stalk at $x$, and $I := c(\mathfrak m_A)\mathcal O_{X,x}$ for the ideal generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $A$. Then $\mathcal O_{X,x}/I$ is an integral domain, a principal ideal ring, and not a field; and every $b \in \mathcal O_{X,x}$ satisfies $b - c(a) \in \mathfrak m_x$ for some $a \in A$.
--
--   This is the local statement that the special fibre of an integral, locally finitely presented $A$-model of a curve is regular of dimension one at a smooth closed point — the conclusion being the defining conjunction for a discrete valuation ring rather than the Mathlib predicate itself — together with the rationality of such a point, i.e. surjectivity of $A \to \mathcal O_{X,x}/\mathfrak m_x$, which comes from the residue field of $A$ being algebraically closed. It is used in the construction of semistable models, being cited by the results on finitely presented localisations of local rings at smooth points and on the shape of the maximal ideal at points where the order is one.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_SemistableModel_isPrincipalIdealRing_stalk_quotient_map_maximalIdeal_of_mem_smoothLocus.lean

